      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <li>Physical DC shunt measured_j, Wearable-MoL vs. smart-glasses micro-LLMs, LastExam-protocol calibration, ISCA 2025 antisymmetric-40 T-MAC, live Alif E3 Cortex-M55 DWT cycles, 15.31 KB lut6_core.wasm, 4-ISA bare-metal MCU ELFs, 4-vendor GPU CubeCL parity, Oct–Nov 2026 looped models, 120B, multi-repo SWE-bench, and reported_j results: Texas Instruments INA3221 (VDD_CPU_SOC_MSS) and INA238 (VIN) DC current shunts on NVIDIA Jetson AGX Thor (Claims LA-24, LA-28, LA-32, LA-33 &amp; LA-38, board_metered = true: 87.25× bit-sliced lut6-core at 162.71 nJ/op, 222.57× wearable 56-bit 4-token epistemic gate at 2,803.25 vs. 623,920.52 nJ/op vs. 1/16th uLM-28M layer, 1.65× antisymmetric-40 zero-MUL T-MAC tail at 8,594.93 nJ/op, 3.74× Sub1Bit-LUT6, 34.21× Expert-AirMoL, and 10.94× Proposition 1 downward-compilation energy reductions with empirical break-even Delta T* = 0.108 &lt; 1 episode), AMD Ryzen AI Max+ 395 Zen 5 RAPL (where Antisym-40 flips Zen 5 from 0.68× to 1.12× CpJ vs. INT8 Micro-MLP at 27,829.94 nJ/op, board_metered = false), live attached Alif Ensemble E3 (OpenMV-AE3 Cortex-M55 @ 400 MHz, board_metered = false: 1.399 µs / 556.94 DWT cycles wearable 56-bit epistemic gate [2,745.18× faster than 1/16th uLM-28M layer], 1.720 µs / 684.57 DWT cycles scalar [173.83×], 26.66 µs / 10,655.8 cycles cached T-MAC [11.17×], and 6.97 ns / 2.68 DWT cycles bit-sliced [44,403.69×]), Wearable-MoL fitting in 5,984 B (9.13% of 64 KB watch SRAM vs. 13.75 MB uLM-28M INT4) with 97.92% wearable reflex and 0.00% prefix poisoning (vs. 93.75% on UW/Meta collaborative prefix masking, Claim LA-36), LastExam-protocol evaluation across 32 open SuperGPQA hard MC10 + AIME/HMMT 2025 Olympiad items cutting RMS calibration error 5.37× (70.62% to 13.14%), driving CHR@80 from 81.25%–96.88% to 0.00%, and lifting selective accuracy 2.13× to 40.00% (Claim LA-37), 8-target #![no_std] cross-compilation including 15.31 KB browser lut6_core.wasm (Claim LA-35), October–November 2026 looped models (thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Mini 3.52× speedup / 4.29× lower reported_j, Nemotron-Labs-Dory1.0-4B 3.95× speedup at 100% greedy parity), four-vendor Burn 0.22.1 / CubeCL GPU shaders (up to 328.06×), Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B in 970.0 MB RAM (12.30× NVMe cut), measured 120B-A12B (58,075.4 MB RSS, 22.17 tok/s, 62.50% verified pass), BigCodeBench v0.1.3 (90.62%), 40 upstream SWE-bench Verified git-worktree evaluations (0.00% broken commits), and Rust mol-agent-rs (0.154 ms/req MCP; 61/61 pytest pass).</li>
        <li>License-free openXC7 320.62 MHz post-PAR .bit bitstream, cosmic-ray SEU (72, 64) SECDED survival, and Kria KV260 (xck26) &amp; Artix-7 XC7A200T RTL / VCD / DS181 audits: Claim LA-34 closes license-free openXC7 (nextpnr-xilinx 0.8.2 + Project X-Ray) post-route static timing at 320.62 MHz (PASS at 250.0 MHz) and emits a 9,730,768 B (77.846 Mbit) .bit bitstream on xc7a200tfbg484-2 while (72, 64) RAMB36 SECDED + 0x3C apoptosis achieves 100.00% survival and 0.0000% silent corruption at BER = 1.0% (vs. 26.28% / 37.0% NaN on BF16), paired with 64/64 Yosys abc -lut 6 Boolean miter equivalence, 41,465 xcup CLB LUTs (15.59 est_mW CE-gated idle [4.10× cut]), and Claim LA-30's Artix-7 XC7A200T M.2 2280 gateware port (62,211 xc7 LUTs = 46.22%, 365-RAMB36E1 1.46 MB crystal vault, 10,500/10,500 KV260 vector parity, and 0.86 est_W M.2 3.3V @ 55.2 est_C with DDR3 held in CMOS reset).</li>
        <li>Oracle-free wake gate, wobble Fourier vanishing, hle:3r2s canary quarantine, and Inria Charon+Aeneas Rust-to-Lean extraction: 0.00% false crystallization risk and 1.0000 OOD AUROC on the shifted test stream via a radially regularized JEPA-EBRM Split-Conformal + Adaptive Conformal Inference gate, paired with 58 six-kernel-proved Lean 4.36.0 theorems (58,802 con-leche/con-ron --verified declarations; 1,422 fleet theorems) and mechanical Charon+Aeneas Lean typechecking of 6 #![no_std] Rust functions (Lut6Verify_Aeneas.lean), keeping Conformal-bounded distinct from Deterministic.</li>
        <li>Not claimed: direct access to gated cais/hle items (HTTP 403 gate strictly respected with zero bypass), physical Kria KV260 or Numato Aller A7 XC7A200T FPGA board bitstream loading or rail power in this repository (measured_j = None and board_metered = false across all xck26, XC7A200T, openXC7 post-PAR, OpenMV-AE3 cycle, WASM, and cross-compiled MCU ELF rows; §4.22, §4.25, and §4.32 figures are analytical est_j / est_mW / est_C, while physical DC shunt measured_j belongs strictly to Jetson AGX Thor in Claims LA-24, LA-28, LA-32, LA-33 &amp; LA-38), commercial Vivado post-place-and-route 250 MHz timing closure on xck26, silicon energy leadership, or full 500-task SWE-bench Verified container evaluation beyond the 40 real upstream git-worktree evaluations across django, pytest, requests, and sympy.</li>
